    "comparison": "Avian IgY vs Mammalian IgG",
    "why": "Chicken IgY (the functional counterpart to mammalian IgG) possesses a distinct molecular architecture: it has <b>four constant domains (CH1 to CH4)</b> and completely lacks the flexible hinge region present in mammalian IgG.<br><br>The Fc region of IgY lacks the specific amino acid residues required to bind bacterial Protein A or Protein G, and cannot trigger the mammalian C1q classical complement activation pathway, preventing cross-species complement fixation.",
