    "comparison": "Active Immune Rejection vs Mechanical Detachment",
    "why": "In normal parturition, placental expulsion is not merely a mechanical detachment, but an <b>active immune-mediated graft rejection</b>. Fetal cotyledonary trophoblasts express foreign paternal MHC Class I antigens; near term, surge in maternal cortisol and leukocyte chemoattractants recruits maternal neutrophils and macrophages into the caruncle-cotyledon interface.<br><br>These phagocytes secrete matrix metalloproteinases that digest collagen linkages. If maternal cell-mediated recognition is impaired or suppressed by metabolic stress, cotyledonary collagen digestion fails, locking the placenta in place.",
